s moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["BKV Corporation is a small-cap energy business with a $1.9B market cap on $894M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +48% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +50.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $57M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 9.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 67% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 31% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3123877584930002},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Energy peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why (BKV) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/Why_BKV_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_112726123602_1795757762.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795757762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Javier Hinojosa Disposes of 4,952 BKV Corp Shares at $17.54 Average Price","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/javier-hinojosa-disposes-of-4952-bkv-corp-shares-at-1754-average-price","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795541906.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BKV Energy Announces 2026 El